# NestJS Patterns

## Module layout
```
modules/<name>/
  dto/ entities/ <name>.controller.ts <name>.service.ts <name>.module.ts
```

## Rules
- Controllers: routing, DTO binding, guards, Swagger decorators only. No business logic, no repositories.
- Services: business logic; inject repositories via `@InjectRepository`.
- One DTO per request; use `class-validator` + `class-transformer`. Responses use explicit response DTOs, never raw entities.
- Global `ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true, transform: true })`.
- Use built-in exceptions (`NotFoundException`, `ConflictException`, ...) or custom ones in `common/exceptions`. No generic `Error`.
- Guards for auth/roles (`JwtAuthGuard`, `RolesGuard`); decorators `@Public()`, `@Roles()`, `@CurrentUser()`.
- Inter-module access via exported services only; avoid circular deps (no `forwardRef` unless approved).
- Pagination: `?page=1&limit=20`, max limit 100, return `{ items, meta }`.
- Every endpoint has `@ApiTags`, `@ApiOperation`, response decorators.
- Async work (email, expiry) goes to BullMQ processors, not inline.

## Example
```ts
@Post()
@Roles(Role.USER)
create(@CurrentUser() user: JwtUser, @Body() dto: CreateBookingDto) {
  return this.bookingsService.create(user.id, dto);
}
```
